{"id":"05746b7aa62c0d6e82f9d3f47f7263a549a551e3","axis":"silent","repo":"systemd/systemd","sha":"05746b7aa62c0d6e82f9d3f47f7263a549a551e3","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/workflows/mkosi.yml","lines":["@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@ jobs:","           - distro: nura","             release: edge","             libc: musl","-            skip: TEST-92-TPM2-SWTPM","+            skip: TEST-29-PORTABLE TEST-92-TPM2-SWTPM"," ","     steps:","       - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"NEWS","lines":["@@ -89,7 +89,19 @@ CHANGES WITH 263 in spe:"," ","         * systemd-mountfsd now asks polkit if the image policy denies","           setting up Verity, or if the client's image policy doesn't","-          overlap with its own.","+          overlap with its own. It doesn't ask polkit if the client's image","+          policy requires a dm-verity signature that no trusted key","+          validates, because the policy for trusted images refuses such an","+          image too.","+","+        * By default, the image policies that portablectl attach and reattach","+          generate only pin the file system type of each partition, the","+          partition flags and which data partitions exist. The new","+          --pin-protection=yes option also pins the dm-verity protection and","+          the signature of the attached images, as before. With","+          --pin-protection=yes, portablectl attach refuses images whose","+          dm-verity signature the host doesn't trust, instead of failing when","+          the service starts."," ","         * systemd-networkd and networkctl have been merged into a single","           multi-call binary, with the former becoming a symlink to the latter."],"additions":13,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"man/org.freedesktop.portable1.xml","lines":["@@ -323,12 +323,18 @@ node /org/freedesktop/portable1 {","       the safety checks that ensure the units are not running while the image is attached or detached.","       <varname>SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION</varname> will bypass the check that ensures the","       <filename>extension-release.<replaceable>NAME</replaceable></filename> file in the extension image","-      matches the image name. They are defined as follows:</para>","+      matches the image name. For <function>AttachImageWithExtensions()</function> and","+      <function>ReattachImageWithExtensions()</function>, <varname>SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_PIN_PROTECTION</varname>","+      adds the dm-verity protection and the signature of the images to the generated image policies, see","+      the <option>--pin-protection=</option> option of","+      <citerefentry><refentrytitle>portablectl</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>. They","+      are defined as follows:</para>"," ","       <programlisting>"," #define SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_RUNTIME            (UINT64_C(1) &lt;&lt; 0)"," #define SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_FORCE_ATTACH       (UINT64_C(1) &lt;&lt; 1)"," #define SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_FORCE_EXTENSION    (UINT64_C(1) &lt;&lt; 2)","+#define SD_SYSTEMD_PORTABLE_PIN_PROTECTION     (UINT64_C(1) &lt;&lt; 3)"," </programlisting>","     </refsect2>"," "],"additions":7,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"man/portablectl.xml","lines":["@@ -141,9 +141,14 @@","         immediately started (blocking operation unless <option>--no-block</option> is passed) and/or enabled after","         attaching the image.</para>"," ","-        <para>When images are attached, an image policy will be generated that pins the attached image by","-        the exact content that was found while attaching, so that it cannot be swapped downgrading security","-        (e.g.: removing dm-verity protection) without a full reinstallation. For more details on policies, see","+        <para>When images are attached, <command>portablectl</command> generates an image policy that pins the","+        filesystem type of each partition of the attached image, its partition flags and which data partitions","+        it contains. With","+        <option>--pin-protection=yes</option>, the policy also pins the dm-verity protection and the signature","+        that were found while attaching, so that the image cannot be swapped for one with weaker protection","+        without a full reinstallation. In that case, attaching an image with a dm-verity signature fails unless","+        a key in the kernel keyring or a certificate in <filename>/etc/verity.d/</filename> (and related","+        directories) validates the signature. For more details on policies, see","         <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.image-policy</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>"," ","         <xi:include href=\"vpick.xml\" xpointer=\"image\"/>","@@ -326,6 +331,26 @@","         <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v239\"/></listitem>","       </varlistentry>"," ","+      <varlistentry>","+        <term><option>--pin-protection=<replaceable>BOOL</replaceable></option></term>","+","+        <listitem><para>When attaching or reattaching an image, controls whether the generated","+        <varname>RootImagePolicy=</varname> and <varname>ExtensionImagePolicy=</varname> settings require the","+        dm-verity protection and the signature that the attached images have. Takes a boolean argument.","+        Defaults to no.</para>","+","+        <para>When disabled, the generated policies pin the filesystem type, the partition flags and which","+        data partitions exist, and permit images with any dm-verity protection or signature. Images that","+        contain dm-verity data still use dm-verity. If the host doesn't trust the signature of an image,","+        <command>portablectl</command> attaches the image, and dm-verity checks the image against its root","+        hash without validating the signature. With <option>--user</option>,","+        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-mountfsd.service</refentrytitle><manvolnum>8</manvolnum></citerefentry>","+        mounts the image and applies its own image policy, which can still require a signature that the host","+        trusts.</para>","+","+        <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v263\"/></listitem>","+      </varlistentry>","+","       <varlistentry>","         <term><option>--copy=</option></term>"," "],"additions":28,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"shell-completion/bash/portablectl","lines":["@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ _portablectl() {","         [STANDALONE]='-q --quiet --runtime --no-reload --cat --no-pager --no-legend","                               --no-ask-password --enable --now -h --help --version","                               --clean --no-block --force --user --system'","-        [ARG]='-p --profile --copy -H --host -M --machine --extension'","+        [ARG]='-p --profile --copy -H --host -M --machine --extension --pin-protection'","     )"," ","     local -A VERBS=(","@@ -56,6 +56,9 @@ _portablectl() {","             --copy)","                 comps=\"copy symlink auto mixed\"","                 ;;","+            --pin-protection)","+                comps=\"yes no\"","+                ;;","             --host|-H)","                 comps=$(compgen -A hostname)","                 ;;"],"additions":4,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/mountfsd/mountwork.c","lines":["@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@ typedef struct MountImageParameters {","         MountOptions *options;","         bool relax_extension_release_check;","         bool verity_sharing;","+        bool pin_image_policy;","         struct iovec verity_root_hash;","         struct iovec verity_root_hash_sig;","         unsigned verity_data_fd_idx;","@@ -243,6 +244,15 @@ static int verify_trusted_image_fd_by_path(int fd) {","         return false;"," }"," ","+static bool policy_requires_signature(const ImagePolicy *policy, const VeritySettings *verity) {","+        PartitionPolicyFlags f;","+","+        assert(verity);","+